	(text "The pot side of each chip (U7A, U8A, U9A) is drawn on the audio sheets where it acts.\nV+ = 9V and V- = GND, so the pot ends can swing anywhere from 0V to 9V.\nVL = 3.3V matches the microcontroller's logic.  WLAT tied low: a new setting takes effect at once.\nSHDN tied high: normal operation.  At power-up each wiper starts at mid-scale until the\nmicrocontroller restores the saved setting."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.3 144.78 0)
		(effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left))
		(uuid "88f65c5c-45c7-4c12-9fac-68a428224e6a")
	)
